Key sounds for nooxshell: a smooth linear switch, in the style of the
Gateron Milky Yellow set. These are recordings of Alpaca linear switches
from kbsim (https://github.com/tplai/kbsim, src/assets/audio/alpaca),
converted to 48 kHz mono WAV with the leading silence trimmed and 10 dB
of gain:

  ffmpeg -i press/GENERIC_R0.mp3 -af "silenceremove=start_periods=1:\
    start_threshold=-60dB,afade=t=in:d=0.001,areverse,afade=t=in:d=0.004,\
    areverse,volume=10dB" -ac 1 -ar 48000 -c:a pcm_s16le down-generic-r0.wav

press/X.mp3 became down-x.wav and release/X.mp3 became up-x.wav.
Space and Backspace came out louder than the other keys, so they were
then brought down to the same level, measured as the loudest 30 ms:
down-space.wav by 6 dB, down-backspace.wav by 7.7 dB and up-space.wav by
4.5 dB (ffmpeg -af volume=-6dB and so on).

The exception is down-enter-gunshot.wav, the pistol shot Enter plays. It
is "pistol shot" (audio file ID 233473) by mrfriends
(https://pixabay.com/users/mrfriends-45509135/) from Pixabay,
https://pixabay.com/sound-effects/film-special-effects-pistol-shot-233473/
downloaded 2026-11-15 under the Pixabay Content License
(https://pixabay.com/service/terms/), not the MIT license below. It was
trimmed of its leading silence, cut to 1.32 s with a 60 ms fade out, and
lowered to peak at -20 dB:

  ffmpeg -i pistol-shot-233473.mp3 -af "silenceremove=start_periods=1:\
    start_threshold=-50dB,afade=t=in:d=0.001,atrim=end=1.32,areverse,\
    afade=t=in:d=0.06,areverse,volume=-23.5dB" -ac 1 -ar 48000 \
    -c:a pcm_s16le down-enter-gunshot.wav

